Alien LT Wand V3 R3 · geometry and assembly notes
Units: millimetres, grams and gram-force. Right-handed axes: X aft from
the stylus, Y across the wand, Z up from the record surface (Z = 0).

1. Construct the symmetric shell from transverse freeform sections. Retain
   the front crown and the level pickup mounting face at Z = 18.20 through
   X = 37. Use a 24 mm fifth-degree Bezier run-out toward the underside.
   The six Bezier control points have equally spaced X coordinates from
   37 to 61. For the exterior, their Z values are [h,h,h,k-2*p*m,k-p*m,k],
   where h=18.2, p=24/5, m=-0.01223 and k=10.048+(61-100)*m-0.035.
2. Crown the lower length between X = 54 and 190. At the middle of a
   station, lower the original sole by 2.4*[4*t*(1-t)]^3, t=(X-54)/136.
   Fade the adjustment toward the sides and roof. Split the shell on Y=0.
3. Blend the aft transverse sections to a 38 mm wide shell with nominal
   lower/upper corner controls of 5.8/4.2. The aft sole reaches Z=-15.20
   at X=274. The roof levels off at X=298. The tail is semicircular in
   plan about X=286. Finish the side silhouette at X=304.992 with top
   and bottom quarter-round profiles of nominal radii 3.2 and 3.6.
4. Cut the transverse bearing crown, diameter 14.20, about X=237.10,
   Z=+1.50. Blend the front mouth lip to the crown with R4.0. Blend the
   rear lip to the straight lead-in with R4.5. The opening accepts the
   14 mm OD housing from below. The neutral magnet contact lies at Z=0.
   Fit the 34 mm long 14/12 housing, 36 mm long 12/11 insert and two
   lower 4 x 10 magnets centred at Y=+/-10, Z=-2.
5. Fit and bond the vertical 30/28 fixed sleeve at X=286. Its ends follow
   the original shell surface. The two 30 mm diameter mould marks have a
   centre depth of 0.50. File to the actual tube; the CAD bore is 30.20.
   The local upper and lower carbon doublers are bounded by a 4.30 mm
   depth from the local roof and sole reference planes. Fit the two cup
   guides, the internal lock boss, its screw and pressure shoe. The
   service hole opens aft.
6. Assemble the moving cup from 48 mm long 25/23 tube, floor, two crossing
   webs, gasket, lid and lid screw. In the model, 67.89 g of fill gives
   1.75 gf at the stylus with moving centre of mass 0.50 below the record
   plane after vertical adjustment. Set the actual fill by weighing and
   balancing the finished arm.
7. Bond two 46 mm long 10/8 external trim tubes in the nominal 72 degree
   side grooves after demoulding. Moving both nominal 6 g trim masses by
   9.88 mm gives 0.50 gf of fine adjustment. Trial-fit the bearing and
   check the joints, laminate, trim travel and assembled arm sweep.
